   "titulo": "How it forms",
   "texto": [
    "Future of **avere** or **essere** + partition: **avrò finito** (I will have finished), **sarò arrivato** (I will have arrived).",
    "With **essere** the participle agrees: **sarò arrivata** (I will have arrived, she)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "When used",
   "texto": [
    "For a future action before another: **Quando avrò finito, ti chiamerò** (when you are finished, I will call you). In the conversation it is also common to use the present with future value: **Quando avrò finito, ti chiamo**. The previous future also expresses a conjecture: **Sarà già partito** (it will have already gone out)."
   ]
